d":"a1fcbf642815bb01","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/14/#testresult/a1fcbf642815bb01","status":"failed","statusDetails":"Timed out waiting for cluster node \"edge-dev\" to become ready\n\nClaude's conclusion:\n### Root cause\n\nLive evidence on `edge-dev` shows severe host-level storage I/O contention stalling cluster bring-up, not a product bug: `dmesg` shows kernel `hung_task` warnings for `kube-init`, `jbd2/zd16-8`, `jbd2/zd0-8`, `zvol_tq-0`, `z_wr_iss`, and `txg_sync` all blocked for 122+ seconds between 23:21–23:25, and `kube-init`'s own phase log (`/persist/kubelog/k3s-install.log`) shows the `INSTALLING` phase alone took **11m57s** (boot+12m59s) before containerd/k3s even started. By the time `WAIT_K3S_READY → DEPLOYING` fired at boot+18m50s (23:36:15), only ~2 minutes remained before the test's 20-minute timeout at 23:38:25, so kubevirt/longhorn/cdi pods (confirmed live via `kubectl get pods -A`) were still freshly `ContainerCreating`/`Init:0/1` (scheduled only 80–90s earlier) when the harness gave up. Live `top`/`uptime` right now still show 52% iowait and load average ~10 on a 4-vCPU box, consistent with ongoing contention.\n\nThis does **not** share the root cause of this exact test's only prior ledger occurrence (run #12, 2026-11-09): that one was a `kube-init` phase-reset bug where kubevirt/longhorn were structurally *never* deployed. Tonight they were deployed, just too late — this matches instead the broader, well-established \"shared host storage contention\" infra pattern documented repeatedly elsewhere in `live-ledger.md` (e.g. `TestEVEUpgradeKubevirtToKubevirt`, `TestApplicationGateway`, `TestSwitchNIPortConfigRace`), first recorded 2026-10-29 and recurring frequently since — so while this specific test hasn't failed this way before, the underlying mechanism is a known, recurring infra flake rather than a new EVE/pillar regression.","time":{"start":1794350702000,"stop":1794352343980,"duration":1641980}},{"uid":"4241768